Why This Matters
Multihoming is crucial in enterprise environments for several reasons:

Network Segmentation: Different applications can use separate networks for security and performance isolation
High Availability: Multiple network paths provide redundancy and failover capabilities
Performance Optimization: Traffic can be distributed across multiple networks to avoid bottlenecks
Compliance Requirements: Regulatory requirements often mandate network separation for different types of data
Legacy Integration: Existing applications may require specific network configurations that multihoming can accommodate
